# ─── Claude Code: .claudeignore ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose:  Prevent Claude from wasting context on files that contain
#           no code insight — dependencies, build output, static assets, logs.
# Syntax:   Same as .gitignore (glob patterns, ! overrides)
# Scope:    Soft filter — Claude still CAN read these if explicitly asked,
#           but they won't be auto-consumed into context.
# Docs:     github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/19875
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# === Dependencies (huge, no code insight) ===
node_modules/

# === Lock file (auto-generated, 49KB of noise) ===
package-lock.json

# === Build output (auto-generated) ===
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo

# === Version control metadata ===
.git/

# === Logs & diagnostics ===
*.log
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json

# === Static assets (icons, images — no logic) ===
public/
src/assets/

# === Other AI tool configs (not relevant to Claude) ===
.aiexclude
.antigravityignore
.clineignore
.geminiignore

# === OS junk ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.sw?

# ─── KEPT (not ignored — Claude needs these) ──────────────────────────────
# src/             ← all source code
# .claude/         ← Claude Code own config (agents, skills, settings)
# docs/            ← project documentation (tasks, test-cases, workflow)
# memory-bank/     ← project context (brief, patterns, progress)
# package.json     ← dependency manifest
# tsconfig*.json   ← TypeScript configuration
# vite.config.ts   ← build configuration
# index.html       ← entry point
# .gitignore       ← useful reference for what git excludes
# .vscode/         ← editor settings (may contain useful config)
# README.md        ← project overview
# .oxlintrc.json   ← linter rules
